A||||5||Carrolles||85GT front facia peeling back||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||10-24-2000||08:37 AM||||The front fascia on my 85GT hangs up on the hood when I close it.  The lip where it is attached is curled back and catches on the front edge of the hood.<P>I removed the screws and tried to push the lip back in place but it is curled up and is very stubborn.  I'm afraid that if I simply force it back in place and install the screws it will simply pull out again.  If I try heating it to relax it I'm afraid I'llscrew up the paint.<P>Anyone have this problem and found a fix?<P>TIA,<P>Carroll<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 10-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||10-24-2000||11:15 AM||||  Check your hood for misalignment.<P> Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000002||Tigger||10-24-2000||11:47 AM||||I think there's fore/aft adjustment in the sheet metal piece that connects the facia to the body.  You probably will have to remove the hood to get to the torx fasteners that hold it.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||10-24-2000||12:48 PM||||The actual flexible material of the fascia is curled up where it turns down in the gap between the fascia and the hood.  It is curled up enough that it gets caught up on the hood as the front of the hood swings up as it is closing.<P>Is there a metal backing strip embeded in the flexible fascia lip that I might be able to bend back into shape?<P>TIA<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||286SE'S||10-24-2000||03:46 PM||||With the hood up you will see a row of torque<BR>head bolts down in the gap. No, You do not need to take off the hood to remove them. Yes, There is a metal reinforcement attached to the facia and that is what the bolts are holding on. You may want to take off the whole front facia to do your repairs. It isn't hard at all and suprized me the first time I did it. There are bolts under the side markers lights, wheel wells and under the car but after they are removed the whole front just lifts right off! My car is an 86 SE so would be the same as your 85 GT.<BR>I would say low heat (hair dryer?) to reform the plastic and a good glue and clamps to secure it. Be sure to  clean both surfaces before gluing.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||10-24-2000||04:01 PM||||I had started removing the small 7mm hex head screws that I suppose hold the flexible part to the backing strip.  I'll remove the whole fascia and try the low heat.<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
